nodes.body:
@hubertlu-tw @HaiShaw could you please take a look when you have a chance?

This is the compressed-tensors counterpart of the Qwen3.5 MTP loading issue handled in #23146. Instead of disabling quantization for the entire MTP module, this PR exposes the existing fused projection mapping so `qkv_proj` and `gate_up_proj` inherit their component `ignore` entries. The focused CPU regression passes 27/27 locally.

If the direction looks right, could someone with permission also add the `run-ci` label? Thanks!

@HaiShaw @yichiche quick follow-up now that there is independent GPU validation of the production change in this PR: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/35887#issuecomment-5446106644

On a single NVIDIA GB10 with a compressed-tensors W4A16 checkpoint, the patch reduced missing MTP parameters from 5 to 0, improved accept length from roughly 1.2–1.46 to 2.25–3.79, and matched the previous workaround token-for-token. The mapping is still absent from main, so this fix has not been superseded.

Could one of you please review the direction and, if it looks good, add the run-ci label? Thank you.

